    {
      "gate": "Defect reproduction",
      "outcome": "PASS",
      "reason": "On main, each output or path guard tested exists() and is_symlink() together; exists() is false for a dangling symlink, so a dangling link passed the guard and the following write_text/write_bytes created or overwrote the link target. Each guard now tests is_symlink() alone. Affected: the stale-scan, meta-block and document-graph --output writers and the synthetic release catalog closure --write-packet writer. tools/release/rollback_apply.py has the same pattern in safe() but is digest-pinned by release-dry-run and rollback-drill; it is left unchanged here for a deliberate re-pin."
    },
    {
      "gate": "Tests",
      "outcome": "PASS",
      "reason": "One new test per tool creates a dangling symlink at the output and asserts the tool refuses it without creating the target; each fails against main and passes here. The four tools' test files pass."
